ever invent prices, plan names, credit costs, seat caps, quota values, unsupported integrations, role permissions, scoring definitions or technical behaviour. •	Where the PRD says TBD, show a neutral placeholder, configurable field, disabled state or clearly labelled proposed concept. Do not pretend the value is approved. •	Use “Client Admin” for the customer-company administrator. “Super Admin” means the SellMore platform operator. “Client” or “prospect” means the external buyer. •	All panels share a design system but must have role-specific navigation, dashboards, record scope and actions. •	The UI generator must create screen families, details, forms, dialogs, loading and error states, not just a home screen. 2. MASTER GENERATION INSTRUCTION — COPY INTO THE AI UI GENERATOR COPY EVERYTHING IN THIS SECTION  The text below is the primary instruction to the UI generator. Do not shorten it or substitute a generic SaaS dashboard prompt. You are a senior enterprise SaaS product designer, UX architect, interaction designer and design-systems specialist. Create the complete SellMore web application from the attached SellMore Master PRD v1.2 and this UI Generation Specification. Read both documents before designing. The original PRD is authoritative. This is a complete product design task, not a marketing website task and not a dashboard-only task. Generate a connected, high-fidelity, desktop-first responsive SaaS application with detailed screen flows, realistic data, reusable components and interactive prototypes. ABSOLUTE COMPLETENESS RULE: Preserve every confirmed requirement, feature, field, action, workflow, exception, plan restriction, role boundary, acceptance criterion and visual-reference interaction in the source. Do not omit requirements because they appear in tables, appendices, screenshots or decision registers. Do not simplify a multi-step workflow into a static card. Do not invent missing rules. Distinguish confirmed, proposed, TBD and excluded items. PRODUCT STRUCTURE: Create three separate customer panels: 1) Client Admin Panel — customer-company administration, company dashboard, team, company documents and QA prompt access, meeting upload and analysis, billing/subscription and company-level configuration as authorized. 2) Manager Panel — manager workspace limited to assigned Sales Representatives and their permitted records. Provide manager-oriented team/deal visibility and coaching workflows only where supported by the PRD. 3) Sales Representative Panel — personal sales workspace limited to the user's own permitted records, assigned deals, meetings, preparation, analysis, practice, roleplay and Live Assist where entitled. The PRD also defines a separate platform-level Super Admin Panel. Keep it separate from these three customer-facing panels. Its detailed capabilities are proposed and must be labelled accordingly. DESIGN SYSTEM: Build a polished, mature B2B sales-intelligence SaaS interface. Use a consistent deep-navy/blue/white/neutral palette, restrained semantic green/amber/red, highly readable sans-serif typography, consistent spacing, accessible contrast, clean tables, restrained cards, clear hierarchy and realistic information density. Body copy and table text must remain readable; avoid tiny fonts, oversized headings, excessive gradients, decorative clutter and generic placeholder content. Use a collapsible left sidebar, role-aware navigation, top bar, breadcrumbs, search where relevant, notifications and profile/workspace menu. Create reusable tables, filters, tabs, cards, status badges, forms, modals, charts, transcript components, scorecards, deal/stakeholder cards and AI chat components. ROLE EXPERIENCE: Do not merely change the role label on the same dashboard. Each role must have an appropriate navigation structure, home dashboard, data scope and available actions. If a permission is not specified, do not assume access. Mark it as permission TBD and design a neutral access state. Managers must never see unassigned representatives' records. Sales Representatives must never see other representatives' private records. Client Admin is the company-level administrator. Super Admin is platform-level only. JOURNEYS: Design both account/subscription journeys and the sales-execution loop. Include visitor → Start Free → registration → Free Plan → dashboard; visitor → choose paid plan → registration/sign-in → order summary → payment → verified activation; existing customer → billing/pricing → sign-in → plan selection → order summary → payment → activation. Paid features must not unlock before successful payment confirmation. Failed payments must preserve current access. Design sales execution: CRM/manual context → deal → prepare → conduct meeting → capture → analyse → practise/roleplay optionally → follow-up → CRM update where configured → repeat. Also design manual upload when CRM/Drive are not connected. HYBRID DATA EXPERIENCE: A meeting is created once with one canonical identity. It can appear in the Global Meeting Library and, when associated, in the relevant Lead/Deal Workspace. Both routes open the same meeting, transcript and analysis. Do not duplicate records. Keep unassociated meetings in the Global Meeting Library. Group calls only when they concern the same prospect/contact AND the same potential purchase/project. Do not merge unrelated purchases merely because the contact is the same. MODULES: Create the full screen journeys for registration, sign-in, pricing/plan comparison, order summary/payment states, dashboards, Team Management, CRM Integration, CRM Auto Fill placeholder, Google Drive integration/folder selection, Lead/Deal Workspace, Global Meeting Library, meeting upload, six-tab Analysis Report, Deal Assistance, Company Intelligence under Analytics, Deal Coaching Manager and Representative modes, Task Intelligence/Follow-ups, V2 Automations/AI Workflows, Knowledge Base, Practice/Lessons, Mock Meetings/Roleplay, Live Assist Chrome extension, Analytics, Conversational Intelligence/AI Chat Assistant, Billing/Credits/Payments and separate proposed Super Admin reference. MEETING REPORT: Use exactly the 12 ZEDAXIS sales cues from the PRD and exactly six tabs: Overview, Scorecard, Cue Analysis, Objections, Transcript, What to Improve. Use the specified 0–5 scoring descriptions. Every cue needs score, transcript evidence, observation, improvement and severity where applicable. Use “Not Assessable” when evidence is insufficient. Do not score keyword mentions alone. FREE PLAN: Show maximum 10 meeting records, manual meeting upload, Company Documentation, Team Management within configured seat limit, predefined QA prompts view-only. CRM, Google Drive, Practice, Mock Meetings and Live Assist are locked/unavailable as specified. Show locked features clearly with an upgrade path. Do not invent the numerical seat limit. INTEGRATIONS: Salesforce is the V1 CRM baseline; HubSpot is subsequent-release candidate. Free Plan CRM is disabled. Paid access depends on entitlement. Google Drive is paid/entitled and uses a selected folder; manual upload remains available. Show connected/disconnected/authorization/sync/error/re-authentication states, but do not invent sync directions or write-back permissions. CRM Auto Fill fields and direction are TBD. Default initial Salesforce access is read-only until write-back is approved. FEATURE-SPECIFIC RULES: Company Intelligence belongs under Analytics, not Analyse. Task Intelligence and Follow-ups are V2 and Follow-ups remains a separately named item until its relationship is decided. Automations and AI Workflows are V2. Practice is unavailable on Free. Deal Coaching is a multi-lesson programme tailored to one specific Deal and representative performance. Live Assist is Chrome-extension-first and preserves the source's “Tactic” reference label where relevant. Do not include the excluded Kota-branded agent pattern. Kendo is a link-only reference, not a SellMore feature. SCREEN COMPLETENESS: For every module create list/index, detail, create/configure/edit where supported, forms, tabs, filters, actions, confirmation dialogs, and relevant loading, empty, processing, failed, locked, permission-denied and success states. Buttons and navigation must be connected in the prototype. Use realistic sample companies, deals, contacts, meetings, tasks and transcripts. Use clear breadcrumbs and consistent page titles. Include desktop and responsive tablet/mobile adaptations; preserve usability rather than shrinking desktop screens. FINAL AUDIT: Map every screen and interaction to PRD Sections 1–34 and to the requirement traceability register. Produce a coverage report with: PRD section/requirement, generated screen/component, status (covered/partial/missing), and notes. Do not claim complete if any requirement is missing. List all unresolved Product Owner decisions separately. Visual fidelity and feature completeness are both required; completeness takes priority. 3. PRODUCT MAP AND ROLE ARCHITECTURE Layer / role	Primary purpose	Non-negotiable boundary Super Admin Panel	Platform operator; cross-tenant platform configuration	Separate platform layer; detailed capability inventory is proposed, not fully confirmed. Client Admin Panel	Administers one customer company/tenant	Company-level dashboard, team administration, company documents, QA prompt access, meeting uploads/analysis, billing/subscription. Manager Panel	Team-level user	Can access only assigned Sales Representatives and permitted records. Other permissions require the matrix/decision. Sales Representative Panel	Person conducting sales conversations	Can access only own permitted records and assigned opportunities. 3.1 Role-specific navigation blueprint Client Admin navigation	Manager navigation	Sales Representative navigation Dashboard	Dashboard	Dashboard Analyse: Meeting Analyse / Global Meeting Library	Team Deals / Deal Workspace (scope permitted)	My Deals / Deal Dashboard Analyse: CRM Integration	Meetings / Anal